    "https://schema.org/mainContentOfPage": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n\n\t\t\t\t\t \n\n                 \t\n\n\n\t « All Events\n\n\t\n\tThis event has passed.\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\tFlorilège – Huit violes\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t25 June 2022 : 21:30 - 23:00\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tWhat better to do during a pandemic than learn a new musical instrument? And if the chosen instrument happened to be one of the most popular for over two centuries with a huge, spectacular repertoire that can be played amongst friends as well as in concert, so much the better!\nLes Voix humaines was delighted to be awarded grants from both the Conseil des arts et lettres de Québec and the Canada Council to teach the viol to professional baroque musicians. You’ll see some very familiar faces this evening, each musician brave enough to perform their first viol consort concert for you tonight!\nLes Voix humaines foraged for instruments, finding enough to either rent or borrow to make this project possible. Many thanks to both McGill and the University of Montreal as well as several generous individuals for their loans. Re-stringing of instruments, repairs and re-hairing of bows all lead up to the start of distanced, masked lessons! Concerts planned were usurped by various pandemic lockdowns but tonight we present a wonderful concert of varied music from the 16th century.\nProgramme\nM. Henry Noel his Galliard – John Dowland (1563-1626)\nLachrimae Antiquæ – John Dowland\nDuo pour dessus et tenor – Giovanni Coperario (1570-1626)\nSinfonia no 2 – Leonora Duarte (1610-1678)\nRondeau – The Fairy Queen – Henry Purcell (1659-1695)\nFantasia 1 – Henry Purcell\nArt de la fugue – Contrapunctus 1 – J. S. Bach (1685-1750)\nDuo pour 2 basses de viole – J. B. Boismortier(1689-1755)\nConcert pour quatre parties de viole – M. A. Charpentier (1643-1704)\nPrelude 1, Sarabande, Gigue Anglaise,Passacaille – M. A. Charpentier\nPrelude 2, Sarabande, Gigue Française. Passacaille – M. A. Charpentier\nM. Henry Noel his Galliard – John Dowland (1563-1626)Lachrimae Antiquæ – John DowlandDuo pour dessus et tenor – Giovanni Coperario (1570-1626)Sinfonia no 2 – Leonora Duarte (1610-1678)Rondeau – The Fairy Queen – Henry Purcell (1659-1695)Fantasia 1 – Henry PurcellArt de la fugue – Contrapunctus 1 – J. S. Bach (1685-1750)Duo pour 2 basses de viole – J. B. Boismortier (1689-1755)Les Roulades – Sieur de Sainte-Colombe (v. 1640 – v. 1700)\nLes Pleurs – Sieur de Sainte-Colombe\nChacone rapportée – Sieur de Sainte-ColombeConcert pour quatre parties de viole – M. A. Charpentier (1643-1704)Prelude 1, Sarabande, Gigue Anglaise,Passacaille – M. A. CharpentierPrelude 2, Sarabande, Gigue Française. Passacaille – M. A. Charpentier\nArtists\nKyran Assing, Jessy Dubé, Marie Nadeau-Tremblay and Mélisande Corriveau, treble viols\nOlivier Brault and Pierre Cartier, tenor viols\nChloé Dominguez, Eliana Zimmerman and Susie Napper, bass viols\nBUY TICKETS\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\n\t Details \n\t\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\t Date: \n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t 25 June 2022 \n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t Time: \n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t21:30 - 23:00\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\tEvent Category: Concert\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t Website: \n\t\t\t\t\t\t https://montrealbaroque.com/fr/edition-2022/florilege \n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\n\n\n\tOrganizer\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tFestival Montréal Baroque\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\tWebsite:\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\thttps://www.montrealbaroque.com\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\n\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\n\t Venue \n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t Rialto Hall \n\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\n5711 avenue du Parc\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\tMontréal,\n\n\tQuébec\n\n\tH2V 4S8\n\n\tCanada\n\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t+ Google Map\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t Phone: \n\t\t\t (514) 268-7069 \n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t Website: \n\t\t\t\t\t\t https://www.theatrerialto.ca/a-propos \n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\n\n\n\t\n\n\t